# GF180MCU tapeout tree -- what is generated, what is vendored, what is source.
#
# Everything below is re-creatable: PDK copies come back from download_pdk.py /
# volare / ciel, flow runs and build products from the OpenLane 2 flow, and the
# reference repos from their upstreams. The tracked material is the RTL, the
# flow configuration, the pad-ring spec, the scripts and the docs.

# PDK copies and checkouts (hundreds of MB, deep trees)
gf180mcu_pdk/
gf180mcu_pdk_full/
gf180mcu_pdk_dl/
gf180mcu_ol2/
gf180mcu_fd_sc_mcu7t5v0/
pdk/
libs.tech/

# Build artifacts (regenerable); the flow chain scripts in build/ are source
build/*
!build/*.sh
# ... and build/lvs/ is source too: the LVS gate's committed verdict report and its
# README. `!build/*.sh` does not reach into a subdirectory, and an ignored directory
# is not descended into, so the directory itself has to be un-ignored.
!build/lvs/
# ... and build/lvs_fixtures.tsv is source: the manifest the refresh job, the fetcher and the
# gate all read. Without this line it is silently untracked, so CI would check out no manifest
# at all and the family evidence would describe a list nobody can see.
!build/lvs_fixtures.tsv
# ... and the die's LVS probes are source too: the crop that brackets the deck's `align`, the
# deck DSL probe that answers whether `threads` exists, and the per-cell probes. They are what
# doc/lvs_plan.md and the stream-out report cite, and they are small. What the runs write beside
# them -- layouts, netlists, logs -- stays ignored.
!build/lvs_chip/
build/lvs_chip/*
!build/lvs_chip/probe/
build/lvs_chip/probe/*
!build/lvs_chip/probe/*.py
!build/lvs_chip/probe/*.lvs
!build/lvs_chip/probe/*.rb
openlane2_rtl/runs/
openlane2_design/runs/

# Layout and netlist products
*.gds
*.gds.gz
*.oas
*.def
*.odb
*.spef
*.sdf
*.vvp
*.blif
*.stream

# Logs (the per-run logs live inside runs/ anyway)
*.log

# Vendored upstream reference material (re-clone with git)
tools/gf180mcu-precheck/
tools/gf180mcu-project-template/
tools/gf180mcu-example-layouts/
